! TDDFT mode matrix 01/16 -- CIS  (HF reference + TDA)
!
! The Hartree-Fock limit of the TDA branch: no XC kernel is built at
! all (have_kernel = .false.), c_hf = 1, so the assembled A matrix is
! exactly the CIS matrix of Hirata-Head-Gordon.  This case exercises
! the code path with the FEWEST ingredients and is therefore the one
! to look at first when the whole matrix goes red.
%method  HF
%basis   sto-3g
%job     energy
%charge  0
%mult    1
%tddft   3
%tddft_tda on
%tddft_multiplicity singlet
%geom angstrom
O    0.000000    0.000000    0.117300
H    0.000000    0.757200   -0.469200
H    0.000000   -0.757200   -0.469200
*end
